{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1520071-v5-homebrew-ventrue-antitribu-loresheet","id":1520071,"title":"(V5 homebrew) Ventrue antitribu loresheet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-07T17:57:50-07:00","id":1520071,"title":"(V5 homebrew) Ventrue antitribu loresheet","content":"I love Ventrue <i>antitribu</i>, and thought I'd start working up a homebrew loresheet for them. I'd be interested in hearing thoughts, suggestions, balancing concerns, and vibe checks about the whole thing. What I'm presenting at first will be a brainstorm WIP, so bear in mind. My own commentary is in italics.<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of the Blood (Ventrue only)</b><br /> <br /> Rawr we still think it's the 1200's! We don't bring knives to gunfights, we bring swords! Really, really big swords! The two most important words in the English language to us are DEUS, and VULT. In that order. The other Ventrue may think we're atavistic throwbacks and Renaissance Faire LARP'ers, but to that we say LARP DEEZ NUTS.<br /> <br /> <i>(Yeah, I'm shitposting fluff at this point. I need to suss out mechanics first.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Squire of the Knights:</b> You have been initiated into the Knights of the Blood, and are learning to discern the machinations of the Ephorate. If this merit is bought at character creation, you may reallocate a single discipline dot from Dominate or Presence to Auspex; otherwise, you may purchase your first dot of Auspex without having tasted the blood of a vampire with it (you must still feed from mortals of Phlegmatic resonance).<br /> <br /> <i>(Yay, &quot;free&quot; Auspex without having to give up Presence or Dominate, since v5 is -- probably rightly -- anti-&quot;extra clan discipline&quot; shenanigans. But still out-of-clan at this point, if the player wants to hold on to both Dominate and Presence without giving up bloodline flavor. I'm entirely aware this would allow the character to start with Auspex 2 with the right predator type, and that's on purpose.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Schemes of the Masters:</b> Your experience acting as an inquisitor towards your own clan has granted you insight into their methods and goals, and how they relate to the Ephorate and the clan at large. Once per story, you may ask your Storyteller for a single piece of information about the Ventrue in your own city or those nearby, and be given an accurate answer. As a consequence of your actions against your own clan, you gain the Status flaw <b>(</b>\u2022<b>) Suspect</b> with Ventrue loyal to the Camarilla, regardless of your Status with other groups.<br /> <br /> <i>(&quot;Ask Storyteller for X information&quot; seems to be a running theme with two-dot loresheet merits, and I'm not breaking the mold here. If you're taking this loresheet to begin with, you're probably interested in fucking the Ventrue in particular, and free information about local Ventrue and their weaknesses is just the thing for it.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Crusader's Armory: </b>Experience has taught you the surest way to fail in your duties is to be unprepared, and you are rarely without the tools you need to see your duties done. Havens which you inhabit, including temporary and shared havens, gain two dots to split between Hidden Armory, Library, and Security System at your choice. Your hidden armories may also include melee weapons, bows, crossbows, and stakes instead of pistols or long firearms, at your discretion. Additionally, add two dice to Preparedness checks you make.<br /> <br /> <i>(Archaic weapons are just plain better against vampires than firearms, and these vamps know that as well as anyone else -- if not better. Even if their possession risks the Masquerade. Having weapons and texts squirreled away everywhere, and being a vampiric MacGuyver with always having the right tool for the job, fits the &quot;rough and always ready&quot; archetype so well.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Blessed by St. Gustav: </b>You have either participated in the Prayer to St. Gustav rite, or your sire did prior to your Embrace. Select either Dominate or Presence to replace with Auspex as an in-clan discipline. You retain whatever dots you had in the replaced discipline, but you buy additional dots at out-of-clan cost. If you retain Presence, you may not possess the Awe, Entrancement, or Star Magnetism powers; if you already had those powers, you must replace them with Daunt, Dread Gaze, or Majesty respectively. Your associations come at cost, however: you gain the Status flaw <b>(</b>\u2022\u2022<b>) Shunned</b> with Ventrue loyal to the Camarilla, regardless of your Status with other groups.<br /> <br /> <i>(And here we have it, that which defines the Knights of Blood and/or Ventrue antitribu: in-clan Auspex. Except here, because VtR's Nightmare discipline was folded into VtM Presence, I'm letting them keep it at the cost of giving up Dominate. Loading up with the &quot;Nightmare&quot; powers better fits the whole &quot;scary monstrous vampire warlord&quot; archetype the Ventrue antitribu embody better than Dominate, in my opinion. But, they can still keep Dominate if they want.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Duty Before Dishonor: </b>Your dedication to the order, and resolve to see the Ephorate undone once and for all, is unwavering. You grieve the sacrifices you make to achieve that greater good, and move on stronger for the experience. Once per story, you may choose to automatically succeed a Remorse check if any of your Stains were acquired in service to one of your Convictions, or to further your Ambition.<br /> <br /> <i>(The Ventrue antitribu are/were a Sabbat bloodline, and that means doing some heinous shit in contradiction with &quot;knightly&quot; values. Modern nights existence means doing shit in contradiction with &quot;knightly&quot; values. Even &quot;knightly&quot; values as twisted through the hypocritical lens of the Sabbat. You gotta learn to reconcile that, get over your shit, and move on -- and this merit reflects the learned capacity to do so.)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-08-2023, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T20:03:37-07:00","id":1520075,"title":"","content":"I always wanted the Ventrue Antitribu over 'normal' Ventrue, even before V5 so this is definitely a plus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-07T21:22:46-07:00","id":1520078,"title":"","content":"Looks like a cool project. I'll be following this with interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T09:06:38-07:00","id":1520117,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm considering after giving it a sleep, is getting rid of the current two-dot merit, slightly nerfing and shifting the three-dot merit down to two, and replacing it with another. So, it would look like this:<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Crusader's Armory:</b> Experience taught you unpreparedness is the surest way to fail in your duties, and you are never far from the tools you need to see them done. Havens which you inhabit, including temporary and shared havens, gain a free dot in either Hidden Armory or Security System at your choice. Your hidden armories may include melee weapons, bows, crossbows, and stakes instead of pistols and long firearms. Additionally, add two dice to your dice pool when making Preparedness checks.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Victori Spolia</b><b>:</b> Contests and victory are part of a crusader's (un)lifeblood, and you have adapted to claim your due from those you have bested. If you defeat a mortal in physical or social combat and they are not your preferred victim, you may feed from them without spending Willpower. If mortals you defeat in combat are your preferred victim, slake an additional Hunger when feeding from them (you must still kill your victim to reduce Hunger to zero).<br /> <br /> <i>(This really puts Ventrue antitribu in their rightful place as the &quot;evil twin&quot; of warrior-caste Salubri. It could also have cool synergy, role-playing, and story hook possibilities for Ventrue antitribu whose predator types are alleycat, montero, pursuer, roadside killer, or trapdoor -- emphasizing and incentivizing a more violent and martial feeding style than that associated with the Blue Bloods.)</i><br /> <br /> Also, instead of the five-dot merit being a once-per-story &quot;get out of degeneration free&quot; card, I'm thinking this:<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Duty Before Dishonor: </b>Your dedication to the order, and resolve to see the Ephorate undone once and for all, is unwavering. Sacrifices have to be made in the name of the greater good. If you acquire Stains as the result of a bestial failure or messy critical, and your Convictions would mitigate a single Stain, you instead mitigate them all.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 08-08-2023, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}